# Remotion render input for the README hero. Its payload never reached GitHub (this repo's LFS
# budget is exhausted), so leaving it as a pointer makes `git push` fail GitHub's GH008 integrity
# check outright, and `staticFile('captures/ondevice-render.mp4')` would feed the bundler 131 bytes
# of text on a fresh clone. Stored as a plain blob instead (~292 KB). The sibling captures/*.mp4
# predate this and their payloads are already on GitHub, so they stay in LFS.
packages/leclap-brand-motion/public/captures/ondevice-render.mp4 -filter -diff -merge -text

# README/npm artwork, served straight from raw.githubusercontent.com — it has to be the real bytes in
# the repo, not an LFS pointer. This repo's LFS budget is exhausted (see .github/workflows/ci.yml),
# so raw.githubusercontent.com would hand GitHub's camo proxy and npm the 131-byte pointer file as
# text/plain and both would render a broken image. Kept binary (-text) so no eol conversion runs.
.github/media/** -filter -diff -merge -text
